<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/MODEL/" xmlns:dmndi="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/DMNDI/" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20180521/DC/" xmlns:modeler="http://camunda.org/schema/modeler/1.0" id="Definitions_0r7lnm7" name="DRD" namespace="http://camunda.org/schema/1.0/dmn" exporter="Camunda Modeler" exporterVersion="5.41.0" modeler:executionPlatform="Camunda Cloud" modeler:executionPlatformVersion="8.8.0">
  <description>Cervical Cancer Screening

USPSTF Grade A Recommendation (Ages 21-29):
"The USPSTF recommends screening for cervical cancer every 3 years with cervical cytology alone in women aged 21 to 29 years."

USPSTF Grade A Recommendation (Ages 30-65):
"The USPSTF recommends screening for cervical cancer every 3 years with cervical cytology alone, every 5 years with high-risk human papillomavirus (hrHPV) testing alone, or every 5 years with hrHPV testing in combination with cytology (cotesting) in women aged 30 to 65 years."

Population: Women aged 21-65 years with a cervix.

Exclusions:
- Women who have had a hysterectomy with removal of the cervix and have no history of high-grade precancerous lesions or cervical cancer
- Women younger than 21 years
- Women older than 65 years who have had adequate prior screening and are not otherwise at high risk

Design Notes:
- Uses COLLECT hit policy for ages 30-65 to present all three USPSTF-equivalent screening options
- For ages 21-29, only cytology is recommended (single result)
- Absence of cervix (hysterectomy) excludes from all screening
- CDS presentation: single "Cervical Screening Due" alert with tooltip explaining options

Trigger: Encounter-start or preventive care visit.

Glossary:
- AgeInYears: Patient age in years
- Gender: "female" or "male"
- HasCervicalCytologyInLastThreeYears: True if Pap test within 3 years
- HasHrHPVInLastFiveYears: True if high-risk HPV test within 5 years
- HasAbsenceOfCervix: True if hysterectomy with cervix removal or congenital absence
- CervicalCytologyDue: Output — True if cervical cytology (Pap) is due
- hrHPVDue: Output — True if high-risk HPV testing is due

CMS: CMS124 (Cervical Cancer Screening) measures screening completion, not real-time recommendations.

Sources:
- https://www.uspreventiveservicestaskforce.org/uspstf/recommendation/cervical-cancer-screening</description>
  <decision id="Decision_1tr3ohj" name="Cervical Cancer Screening">
    <decisionTable id="DecisionTable_0rek5wg" hitPolicy="COLLECT">
      <input id="Input_1" label="Age In Years">
        <inputExpression id="InputExpression_1" typeRef="number">
          <text>AgeInYears</text>
        </inputExpression>
      </input>
      <input id="InputClause_1sdu1zo" label="Gender">
        <inputExpression id="LiteralExpression_1vml0au" typeRef="string">
          <text>Gender</text>
        </inputExpression>
        <inputValues id="UnaryTests_1onv8ww">
          <text>"male","female"</text>
        </inputValues>
      </input>
      <input id="InputClause_02hxglh" label="Has Cervical Cytology In Last Three Years">
        <inputExpression id="LiteralExpression_145spel" typeRef="boolean">
          <text>HasCervicalCytologyInLastThreeYears</text>
        </inputExpression>
      </input>
      <input id="InputClause_18o8ocf" label="Has hrHPV In Last Five Years">
        <inputExpression id="LiteralExpression_1bo3sz5" typeRef="boolean">
          <text>HasHrHPVInLastFiveYears</text>
        </inputExpression>
      </input>
      <input id="InputClause_hysterectomy" label="Has Absence Of Cervix">
        <inputExpression id="LiteralExpression_hysterectomy" typeRef="boolean">
          <text>HasAbsenceOfCervix</text>
        </inputExpression>
      </input>
      <output id="Output_1" label="Cervical Cytology Due" name="CervicalCytologyDue" typeRef="boolean" />
      <output id="OutputClause_0jiyynr" label="hrHPV Due" name="hrHPVDue" typeRef="boolean" />
      <rule id="DecisionRule_hysterectomy">
        <description>Exclusion: Absence of cervix. USPSTF: "This recommendation does not apply to women who have had a hysterectomy with removal of the cervix." Includes hysterectomy with no residual cervix or congenital absence.</description>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_hyst_age">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_hyst_gender">
          <text>"female"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_hyst_cytology">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_hyst_hpv">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_hyst_absent">
          <text>true</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="LiteralExpression_hyst_cytology">
          <text>false</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="LiteralExpression_hyst_hpv">
          <text>false</text>
        </outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="DecisionRule_0f4sc3c">
        <description>Ages 21-29, recent cytology: No screening due. Patient has had cervical cytology within 3 years per USPSTF interval.</description>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_1mpw0w3">
          <text>[21..29]</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_1n50rfd">
          <text>"female"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_03fopls">
          <text>true</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_1nze03j">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_0f4sc3c_hyst">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="LiteralExpression_0srbvuh">
          <text>false</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="LiteralExpression_0cn56yw">
          <text>false</text>
        </outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="DecisionRule_13vs2cy">
        <description>Ages 21-29, no recent cytology: Cytology due. USPSTF: "screening every 3 years with cervical cytology alone in women aged 21 to 29 years."</description>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_0r5v5q3">
          <text>[21..29]</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_0ecqyva">
          <text>"female"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_06wi1hy">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_1l3g9jz">
          <text></text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_13vs2cy_hyst">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="LiteralExpression_0it64np">
          <text>true</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="LiteralExpression_0p0sfbt">
          <text>false</text>
        </outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="DecisionRule_1dc37ri">
        <description>Ages 30-65, recent cytology: No screening due. Patient has had cervical cytology within 3 years, satisfying cytology-alone option.</description>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_0qzi09q">
          <text>[30..65]</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_17vbkxh">
          <text>"female"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_1aoduku">
          <text>true</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_1g0fbwo">
          <text></text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_1dc37ri_hyst">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="LiteralExpression_04o6wwr">
          <text>false</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="LiteralExpression_00ddf3x">
          <text>false</text>
        </outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="DecisionRule_14awd91">
        <description>Ages 30-65, recent hrHPV: No screening due. Patient has had hrHPV testing within 5 years, satisfying hrHPV-alone or cotesting option.</description>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_0z81m1c">
          <text>[30..65]</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_1t8z0y0">
          <text>"female"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_0htq3y4">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_11o3x5g">
          <text>true</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_14awd91_hyst">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="LiteralExpression_1fy5390">
          <text>false</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="LiteralExpression_0xfs9od">
          <text>false</text>
        </outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="DecisionRule_1emfdg7">
        <description>Ages 30-65, no recent screening: Option 1 — Cytology alone. USPSTF: "every 3 years with cervical cytology alone."</description>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_0khilal">
          <text>[30..65]</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_1pceyxz">
          <text>"female"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_1u3jek7">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_083pgkg">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_1emfdg7_hyst">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="LiteralExpression_1lcupbv">
          <text>true</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="LiteralExpression_0bu8e99">
          <text>false</text>
        </outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="DecisionRule_1b2o303">
        <description>Ages 30-65, no recent screening: Option 2 — hrHPV alone. USPSTF: "every 5 years with high-risk human papillomavirus (hrHPV) testing alone."</description>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_0lbcg9e">
          <text>[30..65]</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_1h7f8ng">
          <text>"female"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_1cyau35">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_145xbqt">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_1b2o303_hyst">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="LiteralExpression_0ykt0mq">
          <text>false</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="LiteralExpression_0rwnhfy">
          <text>true</text>
        </outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="DecisionRule_1fpdvvw">
        <description>Ages 30-65, no recent screening: Option 3 — Cotesting. USPSTF: "every 5 years with hrHPV testing in combination with cytology (cotesting)."</description>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_1l5ylgn">
          <text>[30..65]</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_1iljaz0">
          <text>"female"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_00vzz2f">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_0q60pj7">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_1fpdvvw_hyst">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="LiteralExpression_11wsklx">
          <text>true</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="LiteralExpression_1qo0boo">
          <text>true</text>
        </outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="DecisionRule_0f1cbzv">
        <description>Male: Not applicable. Cervical cancer screening applies only to individuals with a cervix.</description>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_13fbzz4">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_0ex04aa">
          <text>"male"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_0nh7l94">
          <text></text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_09llda4">
          <text></text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="UnaryTests_0f1cbzv_hyst">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="LiteralExpression_0eeth5c">
          <text>false</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="LiteralExpression_0v0cli8">
          <text>false</text>
        </outputEntry>
      </rule>
    </decisionTable>
  </decision>
  <dmndi:DMNDI>
    <dmndi:DMNDiagram>
      <dmndi:DMNShape dmnElementRef="Decision_1tr3ohj">
        <dc:Bounds height="80" width="180" x="160" y="100" />
